				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "Strategy: Aiming to be low impact on the existing code base, while demonstating mild improvements, an alternative (drop-in) Raw™ view (The TM in this context stands for Themed)."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-08-29T10:14:26.838113+01:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-08-30T22:16:58.761029+01:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "Y+95BjRFT9yEecNosqT/Cw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "### Themable\n{{gtMethod:TTApiResult>>ttTheme}} provides configuration to select the class responsible for theming the raw view. {{gtClass:TTOriginalTheme}} maps the original behaviour, but it also gathers and returns \ninformation about the types of items being displayed.\n\nReturning items such as icons together with type information (type -> icon) enables themes to be combined, nested, or overriden in order to negotiate as to how to render a given type.\n### Icons\nIcons in the original \"Raw\" view could be refined. Instances typically display a class icon, even nil, lacks any special treatment.  {{gtClass:TTTacticalTheme}} which uses  #ttType as its main discriminator, maps each type to a suitable icon. \n\n#### #gtIcon\nIs introduced as part of FAMIX but seems under-utilised elsewhere. \nProposal to fixing   {{gtMethod:Object>>#gtIcon}} (and callers) to allow for fallthrough via nil."
			}
		]
	},
